msgid "Infill"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:1220
msgid ""
"This feature automatically combines infill of several layers and speeds up your print by "
"extruding thicker infill layers while preserving thin perimeters, thus maintaining accuracy."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:1226
msgid "Automatic infill combination - Max layer height"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:1228
msgid ""
"Maximum layer height for combining infill when automatic infill combining is enabled. Maximum "
"layer height could be specified either as an absolute in millimeters value or as a percentage of "
"nozzle diameter. For printing with different nozzle diameters, it is recommended to use "
"percentage value over absolute value."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:1237
msgid "Avoid crossing curled overhangs (Experimental)"
msgstr ""

#. TRN PrintSettings: "Avoid crossing curled overhangs (Experimental)"
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:1239
msgid ""
"Plan travel moves such that the extruder avoids areas where the material may be curled up. This "
"is mostly happening on steeper rounded overhangs and may cause a crash with the nozzle. This "
"feature slows down both the print and the G-code generation."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:1246
msgid "Avoid crossing perimeters"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:1247
msgid ""
"Optimize travel moves in order to minimize the crossing of perimeters. This is mostly useful with "
"Bowden extruders which suffer from oozing. This feature slows down both the print and the G-code "
"generation."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:1254
msgid "Use travel optimization"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:1256
msgid ""
"Refine travel ordering with 2-opt improvements after nearest-neighbor chaining. This can reduce "
"travel distance and stringing, but may increase slicing time."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:1262
msgid "Max. 2-opt iterations"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:1264
msgid ""
"Maximum number of 2-opt refinement passes used when travel optimization is enabled. Higher values "
"may reduce travel length but increase slicing time."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:1266
msgid "iterations"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:1273
msgid "Avoid crossing perimeters - Max detour length"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:1275
msgid ""
"The maximum detour length for avoid crossing perimeters. If the detour is longer than this value, "
"avoid crossing perimeters is not applied for this travel path. Detour length could be specified "
"either as an absolute value or as percentage (for example 50%) of a direct travel path."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:1278
msgid "mm or % (zero to disable)"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:1285
msgid "In object force travel over infill"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:1287
msgid ""
"Plan travel moves in object so they preferentially pass over infill regions. Perimeter crossing "
"is allowed. This feature may increase travel length and slicing time."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:1293
msgid "In object force travel over infill - Max detour"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:1295
msgid ""
"Maximum allowed detour percentage for infill-oriented travel compared to the direct path. If set "
"to 0%, the infill-oriented path is always preferred."
msgstr ""

