#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2609
msgid "Stamping loading speed"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2610
msgid "Speed used for stamping."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2617
msgid "Stamping distance measured from the center of the cooling tube"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2618
msgid ""
"If set to nonzero value, material is moved toward the nozzle between the individual cooling moves "
"(\"stamping\"). This option configures how long this movement should be before the material is "
"retracted again."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2626
msgid "Number of cooling moves"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2627
msgid ""
"Material is cooled by being moved back and forth in the cooling tubes. Specify desired number of "
"these moves."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2635
msgid "Speed of the first cooling move"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2636
msgid "Cooling moves are gradually accelerating beginning at this speed."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2643
msgid "Minimal purge on wipe tower"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2644
msgid ""
"After a tool change, the exact position of the newly loaded material inside the nozzle may not be "
"known, and the material pressure is likely not yet stable. Before purging the print head into an "
"infill or a sacrificial object, Slic3r will always prime this amount of material into the wipe "
"tower to produce successive infill or sacrificial object extrusions reliably."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2648 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2705
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4365 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6549
msgid "mm³"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2654
msgid "Speed of the last cooling move"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2655
msgid "Cooling moves are gradually accelerating towards this speed."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2662
msgid "Purge volume multiplier"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2663
msgid ""
"Purging volume on the wipe tower is determined by 'multimaterial_purging' in Printer Settings. "
"This option allows to modify the volume on material level. Note that the project can override "
"this by setting project-specific values."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2672
msgid "Material load time"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2673
msgid ""
"Time for the printer firmware (or the Multi Material Unit 2.0) to load new material during a tool "
"change (when executing the T code). This time is added to the total print time by the G-code time "
"estimator."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2680
msgid "Ramming parameters"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2681
msgid "This string is edited by RammingDialog and contains ramming specific parameters."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2687
msgid "Material unload time"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2688
msgid ""
"Time for the printer firmware (or the Multi Material Unit 2.0) to unload material during a tool "
"change (when executing the T code). This time is added to the total print time by the G-code time "
"estimator."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2695
msgid "Enable ramming for multitool setups"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2696
msgid ""
"Perform ramming when using multitool printer (i.e. when the 'Single Extruder Multimaterial' in "
"Printer Settings is unchecked). When checked, a small amount of material is rapidly extruded on "
"the wipe tower just before the toolchange. This option is only used when the wipe tower is "
"enabled."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2703
msgid "Multitool ramming volume"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2704
msgid "The volume to be rammed before the toolchange."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2711
msgid "Multitool ramming flow"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2712
msgid "Flow used for ramming the material before the toolchange."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2719 src/slic3r/GUI/BedShapeDialog.cpp:52
#: src/slic3r/GUI/Gizmos/GLGizmoMeasure.cpp:2200
msgid "Diameter"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2720
msgid ""
"Enter your material diameter here. Good precision is required, so use a caliper and do multiple "
"measurements along the material, then compute the average."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2727 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7242
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7243
msgid "Density"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2728
msgid ""
"Enter your material density here. This is only for statistical information. A decent way is to "
"weigh a known length of material and compute the ratio of the length to volume. Better is to "
"calculate the volume directly through displacement."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2731
msgid "g/cm³"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2737
msgid "Material type"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2738
msgid "The material type for use in custom G-codes."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2777
msgid "Soluble material"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2778
msgid "Soluble material is most likely used for a soluble support."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2783
msgid "Abrasive material"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2784
msgid ""
"This flag means that the material is abrasive and requires a hardened nozzle. The value is used "
"by the printer to check it."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2789 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7249
