msgid "Material parking position"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4345
msgid ""
"Distance of the extruder tip from the position where the material is parked when unloaded. This "
"should match the value in printer firmware."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4353
msgid "Extra loading distance"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4354
msgid ""
"When set to zero, the distance the material is moved from parking position during load is exactly "
"the same as it was moved back during unload. When positive, it is loaded further,  if negative, "
"the loading move is shorter than unloading."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4362
msgid "Purging volume"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4363
msgid ""
"Determines purging volume on the wipe tower. This can be modified in Material Settings "
"('filament_purge_multiplier') or overridden using project-specific settings."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4370 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4395
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4421 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4431
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6016
msgid "Perimeters"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4371
msgid ""
"This is the acceleration your printer will use for perimeters. Set zero to disable acceleration "
"control for perimeters."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4379
msgid ""
"This is the acceleration your printer will use for external perimeters. Set zero to use the value "
"for perimeters."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4386
msgid "Perimeter extruder"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4388
msgid "The tool to use when printing perimeters and brim. T0 is the first extruder."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4397
msgid ""
"Set this to a non-zero value to set a manual extrusion width for perimeters. You may want to use "
"thinner extrudates to get more accurate surfaces. If left zero, default extrusion width will be "
"used if set, otherwise 1.125 x nozzle diameter will be used. If expressed as percentage (for "
"example 200%) it will be computed over the selected calculation base."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4411
msgid ""
"Base for percentage-based perimeter extrusion width calculation. Used only for percentage values."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4423
msgid "Speed for perimeters (contours, aka vertical shells). Set to zero for auto."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4433
msgid ""
"This option sets the number of perimeters to generate for each layer. Note that Slic3r may "
"increase this number automatically when it detects sloping surfaces which benefit from a higher "
"number of perimeters if the Extra Perimeters option is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4437
msgid "(minimum)"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4444 src/slic3r/GUI/Tab.cpp:2800
msgid "Post-processing scripts"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4445
msgid ""
"If you want to process the output G-code through custom scripts, just list their absolute paths "
"here. Separate multiple scripts with a semicolon. Scripts will be passed the absolute path to the "
"G-code file as the first argument, and they can access the Slic3r config settings by reading "
"environment variables."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4457
msgid "Printer type"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4458
