msgid "Preferred direction of the seam - jitter"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4957
msgid "Distance from brim/object"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4958
msgid "Distance between skirt and brim (when draft shield is not used) or objects."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4964
msgid "Skirt height"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4965
msgid "Height of skirt expressed in layers."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4971
msgid "Draft shield"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4972
msgid ""
"With draft shield active, the skirt will be printed skirt_distance from the object, possibly "
"intersecting brim.\n"
"Enabled = skirt is as tall as the highest printed object.\n"
"Limited = skirt is as tall as specified by skirt_height.\n"
"This is useful to protect an ABS or ASA print from warping and detaching from print bed due to "
"wind draft."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4978
msgid "Limited"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4985
msgid "Loops (minimum)"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4986
msgid "Skirt Loops"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4987
msgid ""
"Number of loops for the skirt. If the Minimum Extrusion Length option is set, the number of loops "
"might be greater than the one configured here. Set this to zero to disable skirt completely."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4995
msgid "Slow down if layer print time is below"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4996
msgid ""
"If layer print time is estimated below this number of seconds, print moves speed will be scaled "
"down to extend duration to this value."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5005
msgid "Small perimeters"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5007
msgid ""
"This separate setting will affect the speed of perimeters having radius <= 6.5mm (usually holes). "
"If expressed as percentage (for example: 80%) it will be calculated on the perimeters speed "
"setting above. Set to zero for auto."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5017
msgid "Solid infill threshold area"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5019
msgid "Force solid infill for regions having a smaller area than the specified threshold."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5020
msgid "mm²"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5026
msgid "Solid infill extruder"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5028
msgid "The tool to use when printing solid infill. T0 is the first extruder."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5034 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6282
msgid "Solid infill every"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5036 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6284
msgid ""
"This feature allows to force a solid layer every given number of layers. Zero to disable. You can "
"set this to any value (for example 9999); Slic3r will automatically choose the maximum possible "
"number of layers to combine according to nozzle diameter and layer height."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5048
msgid ""
"Set this to a non-zero value to set a manual extrusion width for infill for solid surfaces. If "
"left zero, default extrusion width will be used if set, otherwise 1.125 x nozzle diameter will be "
"used. If expressed as percentage (for example 90%) it will be computed over the selected "
"calculation base."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5060
msgid ""
"Base for percentage-based solid infill extrusion width calculation. Used only for percentage "
"values."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5072
msgid ""
"Speed for printing solid regions (top/bottom/internal horizontal shells). This can be expressed "
"as a percentage (for example: 80%) over the default infill speed above. Set to zero for auto."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5083 src/slic3r/GUI/Tab.cpp:2163
msgid "Solid layers"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5084
msgid "Number of solid layers to generate on top and bottom surfaces."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5090 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5091
msgid "Minimum thickness of a top / bottom shell"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5097
msgid "Spiral vase"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5098
msgid ""
"This feature will raise Z gradually while printing a single-walled object in order to remove any "
"visible seam. This option requires a single perimeter, no infill, no top solid layers and no "
"support material. You can still set any number of bottom solid layers as well as skirt/brim "
"loops. It won't work when printing more than one single object."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5107
msgid "Temperature variation"
msgstr ""

#. TRN PrintSettings : "Ooze prevention" > "Temperature variation"
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5109
msgid ""
"Temperature difference to be applied when an extruder is not active. The value is not used when "
"'idle_temperature' in material settings is defined."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5119
msgid "Emit temperature commands automatically"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5120
msgid ""
"When enabled, PrusaSlicer will check whether your custom Start G-Code contains G-codes to set "
"extruder, bed or chamber temperature (M104, M109, M140, M190, M141 and M191). If so, the "
"temperatures will not be emitted automatically so you're free to customize the order of heating "
"commands and other custom actions. Note that you can use placeholder variables for all "
"PrusaSlicer settings, so you can put a \"M109 S[first_layer_temperature]\" command wherever you "
"want.\n"
"If your custom Start G-Code does NOT contain these G-codes, PrusaSlicer will execute the Start G-"
"Code after heated chamber was set to its temperature, bed reached its target temperature and "
"extruder just started heating.\n"
"\n"
