msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5520
msgid ""
"Temporarily close eligible Z-oriented internal openings whose first perimeter would be fully "
"unsupported over a bridge. The printed membrane can be removed after printing."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5525
msgid "Min. hole diameter"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5527
msgid ""
"Minimum equivalent hole diameter to compensate. For non-circular openings, the diameter of a "
"circle with the same sliced area is used."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5534
msgid "Max. hole diameter"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5536
msgid ""
"Maximum equivalent hole diameter to compensate. For non-circular openings, the diameter of a "
"circle with the same sliced area is used."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5543
msgid "Z-hole bridge angle"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5545
msgid ""
"Selects the line direction for the first Z-hole bridge layer. Shortest Maximum minimizes the "
"longest bridge line. Shortest Minimum minimizes the shortest bridge line. Shortest Average "
"minimizes the average bridge-line length. Most Even minimizes the variation between bridge-line "
"lengths. Bridge Angle uses the Bridging angle setting; when that setting is automatic (0), "
"Shortest Maximum is used. Only directions with fully anchored lines are considered."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5547
msgid "Shortest Maximum"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5548
msgid "Shortest Minimum"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5549
msgid "Shortest Average"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5550
msgid "Most Even"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5551
msgid "Bridge Angle"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5557
msgid "Z-hole bridge anchor depth"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5559
msgid ""
"Extends each first Z-hole bridge line only into the lower layer's actual perimeter paths directly "
"adjoining that Z-hole. 0% keeps the bridge at the opening edge. For values below 100%, the "
"locally outermost lower perimeter is left free; the requested depth is rounded to the nearest "
"remaining perimeter, with at least one perimeter reached when two or more are available. 100% may "
"reach every safely available perimeter. A single lower perimeter always keeps edge-only behavior. "
"Outer walls and separate wall groups are not used as anchors. If no more than one third of the "
"bridge lines can reach their requested depth at both ends, the opening is left uncompensated."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5567
msgid "Compensation layers count"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5569
msgid ""
"Number of object layers to close, including the first bridge layer. Tracking stops early if the "
"opening no longer has a unique continuation."
msgstr ""

